From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: pmdomain: rockchip: flag the RK3576 GPU domain as needing a regulator

The RK3576 GPU power domain (RK3576_PD_GPU) is fed by an external
regulator -- vdd_gpu_s0, a buck on the RK806 PMIC -- and, like the RK3588
GPU domain, that supply has to be enabled before the domain is powered
on. If the domain is toggled while the rail is down, the power controller
never acknowledges the transition:

  rockchip-pm-domain 27380000.power-management:power-controller:
    failed to get ack on domain 'gpu', val=0x113ff

and the GPU consumer's first register access then aborts asynchronously,
bringing the machine down:

  SError Interrupt on CPU6, code 0x00000000bf000000 -- SError
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Asynchronous SError Interrupt
    panfrost_gpu_soft_reset+0xe8/0x1d4 [panfrost]
    panfrost_gpu_init / panfrost_device_init / panfrost_probe

The failure is a boot-timing race: an early probe of the consumer finds
the boot-on rail still enabled and succeeds, while a deferred probe that
runs after the regulator core has disabled the unused rail hits a domain
that can no longer power up.

Declare the GPU domain with DOMAIN_RK3576_R(), which the RK3576 NPU
series adds for the NPU domain, so the pmdomain core enables the supply
before powering the domain and disables it afterwards. Boards describe
the rail with a domain-supply property on the pd_gpu node; a board
without one gets a dummy regulator and behaves as before.

This applies on top of rk3576-npu-v14.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -1453,7 +1453,7 @@ static const struct rockchip_domain_info rk3576_pm_domains[] = {
 	[RK3576_PD_NPUTOP]	= DOMAIN_RK3576("nputop", 0x4, BIT(6),  0,      BIT(22), 0x0, 0x18,    0x18,    0x18,    15,   false),
 	[RK3576_PD_NPU0]	= DOMAIN_RK3576("npu0",   0x4, BIT(7),  0,      BIT(23), 0x0, BIT(1),  BIT(1),  0x1a,    15,   false),
 	[RK3576_PD_NPU1]	= DOMAIN_RK3576("npu1",   0x4, BIT(8),  0,      BIT(24), 0x0, BIT(2),  BIT(2),  0x1c,    15,   false),
-	[RK3576_PD_GPU]		= DOMAIN_RK3576("gpu",    0x4, BIT(9),  0,      BIT(25), 0x0, BIT(0),  BIT(0),  BIT(0),  0,    false),
+	[RK3576_PD_GPU]		= DOMAIN_RK3576_R("gpu",  0x4, BIT(9),  0,      BIT(25), 0x0, BIT(0),  BIT(0),  BIT(0),  0,    false),
 };
 
 static const struct rockchip_domain_info rk3588_pm_domains[] = {
